-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",416,{
[13281]="70061FA9\n1\tTalk to someone who might have known the Elven woman\tGurthern has suggested you speak with the Elves who are camped at Sírlond, across the river from Caranost. You should search for Sírlond in central Cardolan.\n",
[13282]="70047BD4\n1\tDefeat Wainrider soldiers (total: 6)\030Defeat Wainrider bowmen (total: 6)\030Defeat Wainrider charioteers (total: 4)\030Defeat Wainrider horsemen (total: 4)\tThe Wainriders can be found at Dol Achcarn in eastern Dagorlad. You have arrived at Dol Acharn and should now defeat the Wainriders to keep them from discovering the Host of the West.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many of the Wainriders at Dol Acharn.\n",
[13283]="700494BB\n1\tComplete A Small Task\030Wait for a slot to open in the pit-fighting tournament\tMaukatish can be found in Thorzhaf. You should either complete a task for Maukatish or wait your turn to get your name added to the pit-fighting tournament.\n2\tTalk to Maukatish\tMaukatish can be found at Thorzhaf. You should speak with Maukatish.\n3\tTalk to Párgrub\tPárgrub can be found near Thorzhaf. You should speak with Párgrub.\n",
[13284]="70040103\n1\tSearch the Hill of Erech for sign of the dark figure\tThe path to the Stone of Erech lies upon the west path out of the southern end of Lancrath. Gúrion has asked you to search the Hill of Erech for any sign of the dark figure he spotted.\n2\tSearch the Stone of Erech for sign of the dark figure\tThe Stone of Erech can be found atop the Hill of Erech in central Blackroot Vale. You have searched the path from Lancrath to the hill and found no evidence of the dark figure's passing. You should now search near the Stone of Erech.\n3\tExamine the strange footprints near the base of the Stone\tThe Stone of Erech can be found atop the Hill of Erech in central Blackroot Vale. You have spotted something unusual near the base of the Stone of Erech and should examine it more closely.\n4\tTalk to Gúrion\tGúrion can be found in Lancrath in south-eastern Blackroot Vale. You have searched the hill, and found strange footprints in the shadow of the Stone of Erech. You should return to Gúrion with this news.\n",
[13285]="700413BD\n1\tClimb the hill to the beacon of Eilendoth\tThe beacon of Eilendoth is located south-west of Ethring in Ringló Vale. You should climb the hill to the beacon.\n2\tDefeat spiders at Eilendoth (total: 4)\tThe beacon of Eilendoth is located south-west of Ethring in Ringló Vale. Defeat spiders at Eilendoth.\n3\tSpeak with Authest\tThe beacon of Eilendoth is located south-west of Ethring in Ringló Vale. You should speak with Authest, the caretaker at Eilendoth.\n",
[13286]="70058C81\n1\tTalk to Nagli Want-kin\tNagli Want-kin can be found at Khadâsh-gâra. Nagli Want-kin and his companions would like to see you off from Khadâsh-gâra. You should talk to Nagli Want-kin.\n2\tTalk to Nagli Want-kin at Khadâsh-gâra\tNagli Want-kin can be found at Khadâsh-gâra. Nagli Want-kin and most of his companions kindly bid you farewell at an unexpected party of sorts. You should talk to Nagli Want-kin.\n",
[13287]="700581A4\n1\t(Optional) Report to a War Effort Recruiter\t\n2\t(Optional) Report to a War Effort Recruiter\030Enter Annâk-khurfu in the Elderslade\tYou are to report to Annâk-khurfu in the Elderslade. Mission Recruiter Stable-masters are available to deliver you there with haste. Mission Recruiter Stable-masters can be found at Thorin's Gate, Gondamon, Bree-town, The Twenty-first Hall, Othrikar, Gabilshathûr, Glóin's Camp, Hrimbarg, Galtrev, The Dolven-view, Magh Ashtu, Járnfast, Erebor, and Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\n3\tTalk to one of the guards in Annâk-khurfu\tSpeak to one of the guards in Annâk-khurfu for directions.\n4\tTalk to Durin\tReport to Prince Durin in the War Room, on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.\n5\tTalk to Glóin\tReport to Commader Glóin in the War Room, on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.\n",
[13288]="700588B3\n1\tComplete 'March on Gundabad: Additional Steps' (total: 4)\tStálskeg Ironbeard has requested your aid in securing a foothold outside of Gundabad for the Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves. He has enlisted Hlóthi to gather several ongoing tasks that need to be completed throughout the area.\n2\tTalk to Stálskeg Ironbeard\tSpeak to Stálskeg Ironbeard to be given a small token of his esteem for your assistance.\n",
[13289]="700587A0\n1\tComplete 'March on Gundabad: Missions for the Cause' (total: 4)\tSeek out and push forward the war effort by completing 'The War Effort: Missions for the Cause' several times.\n2\tSpeak to Elóf\tSeek out and speak to Elóf regarding your completion of several missions.\n",
[13290]="700588AA\n1\tComplete 'Threats to the Battlefield: Svalblóth'\030Complete 'Threats to the Battlefield: Hoshkhor'\030Complete 'Threats to the Battlefield: Grush-and-Flak'\030Complete 'Threats to the Battlefield: Mozlut'\tSeek out the following creatures and defeat them: Svalblóth, the Drake Hoshkhor, the Cruel Barb Mozlut, the Warg Grush-and-Flak, the two-headed troll\n2\tSpeak to Stálskeg Ironbeard\tSeek out and tell Stálskeg Ironbeard of your accomplishments.\n",
[13291]="7005819C\n1\tTalk to Ausma\030Talk to Hórin\tThe dwarves wish to thank you for your hard work! You should talk to Ausma and Hórin in Annâk-khurfu.\n2\tTalk to Durin\tPrince Durin wishes to reward you for your hard work. You should talk to Durin in Annâk-khurfu.\n",
[13292]="70068B26\n1\tRead the manifest at The Drowned Prince in the Sail-haven\tAkhmâra asked you to investigate her business rival. His shop, The Drowned Prince, can be found in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tTalk to Mutâz at the Drowned Prince in the Sail-haven\tThere is nothing suspicious in The Drowned Prince's latest shipping manifest. Perhaps a conversation with its proprietor would yield some clues. The proprietor, Mutâz, can be found outside his shop in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.\n3\tRead the manifest at The Full Belly in the Upper Ward\tMutâz said that Akhmâra is the one guilty of underhanded business practices and has asked you to investigate her. Search for clues around Akhmâra's shop, The Full Belly, in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.\n4\tTalk to Akhmâra at The Full Belly in the Upper Ward\tThe Full Belly's import manifest looks shockingly similar to its rival's. Akhmâra can be found outside her wine shop, the Full Belly, in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.\n5\tTalk to Akhmâra at The Drowned Prince in the Sail-haven\tAkhmâra plans to confront her brother, Mutâz, at his shop. Go to The Drowned Prince in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl to witness the confrontation.\n",
[13293]="7000E836\n1\tScout Ost Galumar\tOst Galumar lies to the north-west of Esteldín, in the North Downs. Handarod has asked you to scout the ruins of Ost Galumar.\n2\tScout Ost Crithlanc\tOst Crithlanc lies to the north-east of Esteldín, in the North Downs. Handarod has asked you to scout the Angmarim-outpost of Ost Crithlanc.\n3\tScout Kar Lak\tKar Lak lies in the hills well to the east of Esteldín, in the North Downs. Handarod has asked you to scout the Earth-kin village of Kar Lak.\n4\tScout Dol Nendír\tDol Nendir lies to the south-west of Esteldín, in the North Downs. Handarod has asked you to scout the ruins of Dol Nendír.\n5\tTalk to Handarod\tHandarod is at Esteldín in the North Downs. You should report to Handarod and tell him what you have seen during your patrol around Esteldín.\n",
[13294]="7006B70A\n1\tTalk to Agalûnu\tShanthar has asked you to return to Agalûnu and tell her to leave Arwáth.\n",
[13295]="7000B403\n1\tTalk to Cannuion\tCannuion is at the Ranger-camp at Tinnudir, in Evendim, to the west of the North Downs. Arohir has sent you to speak with Cannuion in Evendim.\n",
[13296]="7006238D\n1\tDefeat invading wargs (total: 6)\tThe camp is located north-east of Tham Celechir. Defeating the invading wargs may lure the Warg-master out of hiding.\n2\tUse the White Hand Banner to challenge the Warg-master\tCapture the White Hand Banner to challenge the Warg-master and draw him out of hiding. The banner is in the Warg-master's camp, located north-east of Tham Celechir.\n3\tTalk to Rhovandis\tYou have defeated Kalugat, the Warg-master. You should return to Rhovandis in Idhobel and let them know of your success.\n",
[13297]="700033BE\n1\tDefeat Laugfût\tLaugfût can be found among the wolf-pack in the ruins east of Budgeford, beyond Milo and Linda Bolger's farm. Linda Bolger sent you to show the collar to the Elves at Woodhall. Orthir revealed the identity of the mysterious wolf -- Laugfût, a Warg of Angmar -- and asked you to confront and slay the Warg-chieftain.\n2\tTalk to Linda Bolger\tLinda Bolger is in Budgeford, on the road furthest down the hill. Orthir told you to speak with Linda Bolger after you had slain Laugfût. Linda will be pleased to know that the threat of the Warg has been removed.\n",
[13298]="7003EE86\n1\tDefeat Wargs in Hîgropor\tWargs can be found in Hîgropor, in south-eastern Nan Wathren. You should defeat the Wargs and destroy their food-barrels. Fellowship Recommended.\n2\tDefeat Wargs in Hîgropor (total: 10)\030Destroy food-barrels (total: 5)\tWargs can be found in Hîgropor, in south-eastern Nan Wathren. You should defeat the Wargs and destroy their food-barrels. Fellowship Recommended.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the Wargs of Hîgropor, and ensured that they do not return by burning their food sources.\n",
[13299]="7002717A\n1\tBring the ornate spear to Gwilum in Barnavon\tGwilum is at the gate to Lower Barnavon. You should bring the spear you found to Gwilum.\n",
[13300]="700173C1\n1\tHelp Thithrand defeat the Leader of the Warg-riders\030Help Thithrand thin the number of Warg-riders within the Grand Stair\tThithrand is at the Orc-watch. Thithrand is responsible for guarding against the threat posed by the Warg-riders within the Grand Stair. You should assist him by completing his tasks.\n2\tTalk to Thithrand at the Orc-watch\tThithrand is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair. You should return to Thithrand and tell him that each of his tasks involving the Warg-riders are complete.\n",
[13301]="7003E2AD\n1\tDefeat Wargs in Nan Wathren (total: 15)\tWargs from Hîgropor can be found in Nan Wathren, in the southern North Downs. You should slay as many of the foul beasts as can be slain, for they are evil. Small Fellowship Recommended.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of Wargs from Nan Wathren.\n",
[13302]="70052D3E\n1\tDefeat wargs at the clearing (total: 10)\030Defeat Sháraha\tThe Warg Clearing can be found north-west of Vegbár. You should defeat the wargs and their leader.\n2\tTalk to Hertha\tHertha can be found along the road to the High Pass in the Wolf-denes. You should talk to Hertha.\n",
[13303]="7001AB9D\n1\tDefeat Urcheron\030Defeat Carchrien\030Defeat Durkâr\tUrcheron, Carchrien, and Durkâr in Sâd-en-Dagor in Dol Guldur, north-east of Helethir. Torist has asked you to slay Urcheron, Carchrien, and Durkâr, three champions of Dol Guldur.\n2\tTalk to Torist at Helethir\tTorist is at Helethir, south-west from Dol Guldur. You should return to Torist for your reward.\n",
[13304]="70048035\n1\tTalk to Rock\tBy completing this quest, you will receive a Wastes endgame allowance.\n",
[13305]="70042F24\n1\tSpeak with Gladhir\tFaramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath. You should speak with Gladhir at Faramir's Look-out.\n2\tLook at Osgiliath\tFaramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath. You should look at Osgiliath from Faramir's Look-out.\n3\tSpeak with Mírthel\tFaramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath. You should talk to Mírthel at Faramir's Look-out about what you saw.\n4\tLook towards the Morgul Vale\tFaramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath. You should look at the Morgul Vale from Faramir's Look-out.\n5\tTalk to Arodor\tFaramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath. You should talk to Arodor at Faramir's Look-out about what you saw.\n",
[13306]="70062E7F\n1\tCross the river north-west of Sarn Ford and talk to Andy Brockhouse in the Shire\tAndy Brockhouse is the housing broker of Michel Delving, and can be found north-west of Sarn Ford, by the Delving Fields.\n2\tTalk to Thornegil at Sarn Ford\tThornegil is at the crossing of Sarn Ford, south-east of the Shire.\n",
[13307]="70049123\n1\tDestroy fell runes (total: 8)\030Collect rune fragments (total: 10)\tFell runes and rune fragments can be found in the Ered Lithui. You should destroy fell runes and collect rune fragments in the Ered Lithui.\n2\tBring the rune fragments back to the watching stone\tThe watching stone is in Ered Lithui. You should return to the watching stone with the rune fragments you have collected.\n",
[13308]="70018196\n1\tDefeat Cracktooth\tThe Skûmfil is east from the Foundations of Stone. Bassela has instructed you to help a fellow Minstrel complete his or her final task in Skûmfil.\n2\tTalk to Bassela\tBassela is just outside Skûmfil, east of the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone. With Cracktooth slain, you should return to Bassela with news of your success.\n",
[13309]="70019212\n1\tInvestigate Nalâ-dûm for information\tNalâ-dûm is south of the Chamber of the Cross-roads, in the Water-works. Hrólfur wishes for you to investigate the ancient waterway of Nalâ-dûm and recover any lost information about the water-wheels that once fuelled Moria of old.\n2\tBring the records to Hrólfur at the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tHrólfur is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, in Durin's Way. You should bring the ancient records you found to Hrólfur, who will be excited to find a ledger of records of the lore that was lost when Moria fell.\n",
[13310]="7006AD51\n1\tInvestigate Sektakhâb for Khaltâg's wife's necklace\tInvestigate Sektakhâb for Khaltâg's wife's necklace. Sektakhâb is located west of Mekab-kuphâr in Khabârkhad.\n2\tFind and pick up Khaltâg's necklace\tSearch nearby for any sign of Khaltâg's wife's necklace.\n3\tReturn to Mekab-kuphâr to give Khaltâg his wife's necklace\tReturn to Mekab-kuphâr to give Khaltâg his wife's necklace.\n4\tFind Khaltâg's daughter Pharida and share the good news\tKhaltâg has asked you to inform Pharida, his daughter, that her mother's necklace has been found. She can be found working in the Dûlkar, in Dil-irmíz.\n",
[13311]="7006AE8F\n1\tReturn to Khaltâg in Mekab-kuphâr and relay Pharida's message\tReturn to Khaltâg in Mekab-kuphâr and relay Pharida's message.\n2\tAsk Muntâkh if he knows where Khaltâg went\tAsk Muntâkh, the merchant, if he knows where Khaltâg went.\n3\tInvestigate Sektakhâb for signs of Khaltâg\tInvestigate Sektakhâb for signs of Khaltâg.\n4\tAsk Khaltâg why he came to Sektakhâb\tAsk Khaltâg why he came to Sektakhâb.\n",
[13312]="7006B07E\n1\tSpeak with Khaltâg\tSpeak with Khaltâg.\n2\tSpeak with Khaltâg\tSpeak with Khaltâg.\n3\tDefeat Sektakhâb Dead (total: 4)\tProtect Khaltâg and fight off the crypt-walkers that have appeared!\n4\tAid Khaltâg\tAid Khaltâg.\n5\tSpeak with Khaltâg\tSpeak with Khaltâg.\n6\tPick up the heavy necklace\tPick up the heavy necklace.\n7\tThrow the necklace into the Bay from the wharf past the harbour-warden's tower\tGo to the Sail-haven. On the western docks past the Harbour-warden's tower there is a wharf jutting into the Bay. The deep waters of the Bay of Belfalas should hide the necklace for an age.\n8\tSpeak with Pharida about the fate of her father\tSpeak with Pharida in the Dûlkar in Dil-irmíz about the fate of her father.\n",
})
